# config/llama-server-re.env
# Configuration for the llama-server inference backend (re slot -- P40 eGPU).
# This file is read by systemd's EnvironmentFile directive.
# The model manager updates MODEL_PATH when swapping models on this slot.
#
# Deployed at /etc/llama/llama-server-re.env with the P40's real UUID (see
# CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES below); config/manager.env lists `re` in SLOTS. See
# docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-23-dual-gpu-three-slot-design.md Phase 4.

# Path to the GGUF model file to load on startup.
#
# Qwen3.6-35B-A3B (unsloth UD-IQ4_NL_XL, 18.16 GiB) since 2026-10-04. Chosen
# by benchmark over gemma-4-26b-a4b, Qwen3.5-35B-A3B, Qwen3-Coder-30B-A3B and
# Devstral-Small-2 on this card: 10/10 on opencode editor tasks, the fastest
# prefill and generation past 8k of context, and the only candidate besides
# gemma to fit the full 131072 context on the P40. Consumers request it by
# this file's stem (PARE's default model, opencode's editor agent) -- the
# manager answers 409 for any other name, so change those together with this.
MODEL_PATH=/opt/llama/models/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-UD-IQ4_NL_XL.gguf

# Sampling flags for whatever MODEL_PATH points at, read by $SAMPLING_ARGS in
# the unit. They live here rather than in ExecStart because this slot is
# swappable: the manager rewrites MODEL_PATH above on a /swap, and sampling
# tuned for one model is wrong for the next. Change both lines together.
#
# Values below are Qwen3.6-35B-A3B's published "thinking mode, precise coding"
# recommendation from its model card: temp 0.6, top-p 0.95, top-k 20,
# presence-penalty 0. Its general thinking preset differs (temp 1.0,
# presence-penalty 1.5) -- this slot serves agentic code editing, hence these.
#
# MUST stay unbraced in ExecStart: systemd word-splits $VAR but passes ${VAR}
# as one argument. Empty expands to no arguments and llama.cpp's own defaults
# apply, which are not this model's.
SAMPLING_ARGS=--temp 0.6 --top-p 0.95 --top-k 20 --presence-penalty 0.0

# CUDA device selector. Mirrors config/llama-server.env's DEVICE: CUDA0 names
# an enumeration position, not a card, and is only unambiguous because
# CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES below restricts this process to exactly one physical
# card. See that file's DEVICE comment and the device-pinning section of
# docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-23-dual-gpu-three-slot-design.md.
DEVICE=CUDA0

# Restricts this process to the P40 by UUID -- see config/llama-server.env's
# CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES comment for why an ordinal is not sufficient. Get it
# with:
#   nvidia-smi --query-gpu=uuid,pci.bus_id,name --format=csv
# and pick the row named "Tesla P40" (the other row is the V100, which
# belongs to config/llama-server.env, not this file). Set
# CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=GPU-<that uuid> in the deployed copy of this file at
# /etc/llama/llama-server-re.env. Never commit a real UUID here -- it is
# specific to one physical card in one machine. The placeholder below is
# intentionally invalid so this service fails loudly rather than silently
# landing on the wrong card if deployed unedited.
CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=GPU-<uuid-of-the-p40-see-comment-above>

# Number of model layers to offload to GPU. -1 = all.
#
# "All layers" is not "all weights": llama.cpp's load-time auto-fit keeps a
# 1024 MiB free margin and, if the model would breach it, silently moves MoE
# expert tensors to system RAM while still reporting every layer offloaded.
# Observed twice on 2026-10-03/04: Qwen3-Coder-30B at 64k context lost 5
# layers' experts to RAM, and this slot started while another process held
# the P40 and loaded almost entirely into RAM (708 MiB on the card, 4.8 tok/s
# instead of ~47). Check after any start: `nvidia-smi` should show ~21 GiB on
# the P40, and the fit decision is in the log as `common_params_fit_impl`
# lines (needs -lv 5 on this build).
N_GPU_LAYERS=-1

# Work around a CUDA-backend leak where CUDA graphs are cached per
# generation and not freed, growing host RAM under sustained load
# (llama.cpp issue #20315). See config/llama-server.env for the same note;
# left enabled here as the conservative choice pending its own remeasurement
# on this slot.
GGML_CUDA_DISABLE_GRAPHS=1

# Context window size in tokens.
#
# Measured, not projected. Qwen3.6-35B-A3B keeps a KV cache on only 10 of its
# 40 layers (3 Gated DeltaNet : 1 gated attention), 2 KV heads x 256 dims, so
# ~20 KiB/token. llama-server's own accounting at this value:
#
#   llama_kv_cache: size = 2560.00 MiB (131072 cells, 10 layers, 1/1 seqs)
#   common_params_fit_impl: will leave 1767 >= 1024 MiB of free device memory
#
# i.e. 18071 MiB weights + 2560 MiB KV + compute, everything on the GPU with
# ~1.7 GiB to spare. Re-derive from those two log lines after any model change
# rather than scaling the number.
CTX_SIZE=131072

# Bind address and port. Always localhost -- the model manager is the
# public-facing endpoint.
HOST=127.0.0.1
PORT=8084
